# src/common

Cross-pack helpers (`deterministic-reader`, `generate-context`, `generate-entry`, `fill`, `yaml-node`, `yaml-entry`, `specification`, `compile-filter`) live in `@deterministic-code/generators-common`. Import them from that package. Do not re-export them from this repo.

Keep pack-specific modules here: `paths.ts` and `type-converter.ts`. YAML parsing (`specification-parser`, `parse-*`) lives in generators-common. HTTP path casing (kebab segments, camel params) lives in this pack's `paths.ts`. Do not copy generators-common sources back into this repo. Do not put new files under `src/sdk/`.

`generate` is the only export each lane has. It takes `GenerateContext`: `{ reader, settings }` where `reader` is `{ read, exists }` (`IDeterministicReader`) and `settings` is the flat string dict (`application_name`, …). The host never supplies pack-normalized types — each lane's exported `generate` reads YAML and parses once via `DeterministicParser`. Emit logic lives in an internal `generateFrom(deterministic, settings)` that reads `IDeterministic` (`services`, `routes`, `datasourceSeeds`) and treats `expandedDatasourceTypes` / `expandedViewTypes` as the final field lists. Map those fields as-is — do not strip StandardTable columns or rebuild lists with `tableFields` or `parentFields`. Authored `datasourceTypes` / `viewTypes` are for metadata (inherits, enrichments, omit) only. Do not add per-lane aliases (`generateBackendApp`, `generateDatasourceTypes`, …) or host flags (`pinProjectRoot`, `rustModuleWiring`, `assembleAfterStep`). Import `GenerateEntry` from `@deterministic-code/generators-common/generate-entry`, not from a lane module.
